    "title": "The Malcolm in the Middle Reboot Features a Nonbinary Sibling",
    "text": "David Bukach/Getty ImagesLife might be unfair, but LGBTQ+ representation isn’t.While fans of Malcolm in the Middle are most likely familiar with the three male children to Hal (Bryan Cranston) and Lois (Jane Kaczmarek), the reboot, subtitled Life’s Still Unfair, has introduced a brand-new nonbinary character, a younger sibling named Kelly.In the reboot, which premieres April 10, Hal and Lois have a teenager who is much younger than the three characters from the original series, Malcolm (Frankie Muniz), Francis (Christopher Kennedy Masterson), and Reese (Justin Berfield). The newest child, Kelly (Vaughan Murrae) is not only nonbinary, but is also played by a nonbinary actor, who uses they/them pronouns, per their Instagram.“Three out of four of our kids are queer, and without making it a thing and without making an issue, I think it’s really nice to have a character that, that’s just a facet of their personality as opposed to the entire story,” executive producer Tracy Katsky told Deadline.Hulu's \"Malcolm In The Middle: Life's Still Unfair\" New York PremiereVaughan MurraeCindy OrdCreator Linwood Boomer, Katsky’s husband, added, “Also, I mean, it’s in there because I don’t know what else to write except the stuff that’s really happening around me.”Kelly has many of the same personality traits as their older brothers — “intelligent and capable but a somewhat selfish trickster,” per People. An early plotline sees Kelly fighting with their older brother, Reese, to see who can best the other in a battle of reputation ruining.Murrae, who has previously starred in the Hallmark Channel show The Way Home, posted about the Malcolm reboot’s debut on Instagram on Thursday.*Heated Rivalry* May Split Next Book in Two, Just Like *Twilight* and No Other YA FranchiseSeriously, we can’t think of a single other example…“What a time! I was there and then suddenly I was home again. I consider myself extremely lucky to have met such an amazingly kind, hilarious, and creative bunch of individuals,” they wrote. “Working with you all has been a dream, and tomorrow, we get to share that with the world.”Get the best of what’s queer. Sign up for Them’s weekly newsletter here.Originally Appeared on them.",
